# SafeStrip Backend

## Run backend locally

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

## Mosquitto MQTT (local)

This project publishes dashboard events to MQTT topic:

`safestrip/device/{device_id}/dashboard`

### Option A: Run Mosquitto with Docker (recommended)

From project root:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.mosquitto.yml up -d
```

This starts Mosquitto with:

- MQTT TCP listener on port `1883` (for backend publisher)
- MQTT WebSocket listener on port `9001` (for Expo frontend subscriber)

Config file: `Backend/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf`

### Backend `.env` settings for local Mosquitto

```env
MQTT_ENABLED=true
MQTT_BROKER_HOST=127.0.0.1
MQTT_BROKER_PORT=1883
MQTT_TLS=false
MQTT_CLIENT_ID=safestrip-api
# MQTT_USERNAME=
# MQTT_PASSWORD=
```

### Frontend `.env` settings for local Mosquitto WebSocket

Use your machine IP instead of localhost when testing from a physical device:

```env
EXPO_PUBLIC_MQTT_WS_URL=ws://<YOUR_LOCAL_IP>:9001
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MQTT_USER=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MQTT_PASS=
```

Example:

```env
EXPO_PUBLIC_MQTT_WS_URL=ws://192.168.2.12:9001
```
